{
  "id": "T-294",
  "milestone": "M2",
  "depends_on": [],
  "title": "CI passes in a checkout that has no design/tasks directory, so the tracked task specs can leave git in one commit",
  "public_title": "Let CI run without committed task specs",
  "scope": [
    "bin/ci.sh",
    "tests/e2e/**",
    "tests/retro.test.sh",
    "tests/fixtures/**",
    "tests/ci-lints.test.sh",
    "tests/lib/**",
    "design/design.md",
    "design/tasks/T-294.json"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "Why. New task specs have been local, git-ignored files since the change that stopped committing them (T-256), but 231 older specs are still tracked in git. While they stay tracked, the worker keeps extra code that guards them. The captain approved removing them from git in one commit (retrospective item self/R4, card D-1042). Today that commit would make CI red, because three CI checks read this repository's own design/tasks directory from a fresh checkout.",
    "What, fast stage. In the fast stage, the task-DAG check (the check that every task file parses and that every dependency exists without a cycle) prints a skip line and passes when this repository's own task directory is missing, the same way it already skips a missing task directory of an external project.",
    "When this repository's task directory is present, including on open task branches and in worker checkouts that still contain the tracked specs, the check runs exactly as today.",
    "Accepted cost: once the specs leave git, CI no longer checks this repository's tasks, and a wrong self `tasks:` path in `config.yaml` is skipped instead of failing; only local runs check them.",
    "What, end-to-end fixture. The end-to-end test fixture builds its task list from task specs written by the test itself, not from the repository's design/tasks directory. Every end-to-end test keeps its name and what it asserts.",
    "What, retro test. The two assertions in `tests/retro.test.sh` that read this repository's `design/tasks/T-230.json` (`an old pinned spec explanation still validates unchanged` and `a spec explanation never carries retro items`) read a copy of that spec kept as a test fixture instead. Each assertion keeps its name and what it asserts.",
    "Done, tests. A new test runs the fast stage on a fixture tree whose `config.yaml` registers this repository (`repo: .`) with a `tasks` directory that does not exist. It requires exit 0 and a skip line in the existing `(skipped)` format that names the missing self task directory. The test is named `ci: self task directory absent is skipped`, and it fails on the base.",
    "Done, whole run. `bin/ci.sh` passes in a checkout of this branch with design/tasks deleted, and both the end-to-end suite and the retro suite run in that pass.",
    "Docs, CI. design/design.md §10 (CI) says CI does not need committed task specs.",
    "Docs, task DAG. design/design.md §14 (The task DAG) says the DAG stage skips a missing self task directory with a skip line, and no longer says that a CI checkout holds the tracked specs.",
    "Out of scope: removing the tracked specs from git (firstmate makes that commit after this task merges); removing the worker's code that guards tracked specs (a later task); changing the scope gate, which keeps refusing a task spec in a diff."
  ],
